# Risks, Assumptions and Dependencies

## Risks

| ID | Risk | Likelihood | Impact | Mitigation |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| R1 | Identity vendor API downtime or slow responses | Medium | High | Queue and retry; fallback to manual review; vendor SLA |
| R2 | Fraudsters exploit digital onboarding (synthetic IDs, spoofed selfies) | Medium | High | Liveness detection, risk scoring, velocity checks, security review |
| R3 | Regulatory non-compliance (FICA / POPIA) | Low | Very high | Compliance co-designs rules; legal review before launch; audit logging |
| R4 | Low adoption by customers without smartphones or data | Medium | Medium | Branch-assisted onboarding (US-11); keep branch channel |
| R5 | Core-banking API limitations delay integration | Medium | High | Early technical spike; API contract agreed in Sprint 1 |
| R6 | Branch staff resist change | Medium | Medium | Involve consultants early; reposition role towards advice |
| R7 | Poor photo quality causes high referral rates | High | Medium | On-screen guidance, automatic quality checks, usability testing |
| R8 | Straight-through target of 85% not achieved | Medium | Medium | Monitor referral reasons weekly and tune thresholds |

## Assumptions

- A1: Baseline figures in the README are illustrative and would be replaced by real figures from bank data.
- A2: An external identity-verification vendor is available and contracted.
- A3: The core banking system exposes APIs to create customers and accounts.
- A4: The target market has a high rate of smartphone ownership.
- A5: Compliance accepts automated KYC for low-risk applicants within agreed thresholds.

## Dependencies

- Contract and API access for the identity-verification vendor
- Core-banking API access and test environment
- Compliance sign-off on risk thresholds and referral rules
- Legal approval of the e-signature process
- Cloud hosting and security approval

## Out of scope for this release
- Business accounts and joint accounts
- Credit products (overdrafts, loans, credit cards)
- Physical card delivery tracking
- Non-South-African ID documents (to be considered later)
